From 27346193039e8b67f0a203315637a796fe2fe745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:25:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 128/134] feat(pypto-x): execute the torch linear bridge on the
 packed plane (W8J J1.1)

Switch pypto/framework from the legacy ptx_avx512_matmul_<dtype> symbol to the
W8B packed/blocked plane: the weight handle is now the native 64x64 tile
payload produced by ptx_avx512_pack_matmul_{f32,bf16} and the hot path calls
ptx_avx512_matmul_packed_{f32,bf16}.

- weight_pack: handle v2 (layout id, tile element count), native packer is the
  single source of truth for the layout; numpy stays out of the import path.
- linear_kernel: require exactly one packed matmul contract in the artifact,
  cross-check the recomputed contract against artifact metadata, and execute
  the same contract's gemm/pack kernels. declared_plane == executed_plane ==
  packed is an invariant. The cache key gains the packed contract envelope and
  key_version=2, so J1 legacy-plane sidecars are a natural miss.
- torch_ops: pack_weight writes the native tile payload directly into the
  handle; linear_prepacked parses and runs it.
- tests: plane pin => packed, packed==legacy bitwise matrix, native tile
  layout reference, J1 sidecar natural miss, tile constants pinned to the
  compiler/runtime.
